// Oscillating -- the RA-vs-WRA separating behaviour.
//
// rmm-zoo edge: RA strictly weaker than WRA (i.e. WRA is the weaker model).
// Source: Lahav & Boker, "What's Decidable about Causally Consistent Shared
//         Memory?" (TOPLAS 2022), Ex. 3.7 (Oscillating); Lahav, Giannarakis &
//         Vafeiadis, POPL 2016.
//         Vendored shape: rmm-zoo litmus/strictly-weaker/RA-vs-WRA/Oscillating.
//
// One reader sees x go 1, then 2, then 1 again, while two writers each write
// once. Under RA and SRA the reader's three reads are hb-ordered and mo totally
// orders the two writes, so returning to 1 after seeing 2 violates
// read-coherence. WRA has no mo, and the two writes are hb|loc-unrelated, so
// nothing forbids the oscillation.
//
// Reference verdicts: WRA ALLOWS. RA, SRA, C11, RC11 and SC FORBID
//                     (this is a coherence violation for any model with mo).
x := 0;
{
  x.store(1, rel)
} ||| {
  r0 := x.load(acq);
  r1 := x.load(acq);
  r2 := x.load(acq)
} ||| {
  x.store(2, rel)
}
%%
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 2 && r2 = 1) [RA]
